<article class="env-lemma" id="0AUK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AUK">Lemma <span data-tag="0AUK">10.72.11</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $R \to S$ be a finite ring map. Let $\mathfrak m_1, \ldots , \mathfrak m_ n$ be the maximal ideals of $S$. Let $N$ be a finite $S$-module. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \min \nolimits _{i = 1, \ldots , n} \text{depth}(N_{\mathfrak m_ i}) = \text{depth}_\mathfrak m(N)  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemmas <a href="/tag/00GT" data-tag="00GT">10.36.20</a>, <a href="/tag/00GU" data-tag="00GU">10.36.22</a>, and Lemma <a href="/tag/05DR" data-tag="05DR">10.36.21</a> the maximal ideals of $S$ are exactly the primes of $S$ lying over $\mathfrak m$ and there are finitely many of them. Hence the statement of the lemma makes sense. We will prove the lemma by induction on $k = \min \nolimits _{i = 1, \ldots , n} \text{depth}(N_{\mathfrak m_ i})$. If $k = 0$, then $\text{depth}(N_{\mathfrak m_ i}) = 0$ for some $i$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00LW" data-tag="00LW">10.72.5</a> this means $\mathfrak m_ i S_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ is an associated prime of $N_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ and hence $\mathfrak m_ i$ is an associated prime of $N$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/05BZ" data-tag="05BZ">10.63.16</a>). By Lemma <a href="/tag/05DZ" data-tag="05DZ">10.63.13</a> we see that $\mathfrak m$ is an associated prime of $N$ as an $R$-module. Whence $\text{depth}_\mathfrak m(N) = 0$. This proves the base case. If $k > 0$, then we see that $\mathfrak m_ i \not\in \text{Ass}_ S(N)$. Hence $\mathfrak m \not\in \text{Ass}_ R(N)$, again by Lemma <a href="/tag/05DZ" data-tag="05DZ">10.63.13</a>. Thus we can find $f \in \mathfrak m$ which is not a zerodivisor on $N$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00LL" data-tag="00LL">10.63.18</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/090R" data-tag="090R">10.72.7</a> all the depths drop exactly by $1$ when passing from $N$ to $N/fN$ and the induction hypothesis does the rest. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>